  "note": "Triennial election of the Ballycastle Urban District Council, polled Friday 15 January 1932. Seventeen candidates contested twelve seats (six for five in the South Ward, eleven for seven in the North); 92 per cent polled. The new Council was nine Nationalists and three Unionists (Belfast News-Letter, 18 January 1932, p. 9). Eleven candidates for seven seats."
